Mastodon on FenrirOS
====================

Mastodon lives in /opt/mastodon, owned by the mastodon user. Three dinit
services, none enabled: mastodon-web (127.0.0.1:3000), mastodon-sidekiq and
mastodon-streaming (127.0.0.1:4000). Commands run through /usr/lib/mastodon/run
(it loads /etc/mastodon/env.production). Nothing is set up for you: no
database, no secrets, no account, no site.

Needs PostgreSQL and Valkey/Redis (Elasticsearch/OpenSearch is optional).

1. PostgreSQL: createuser -d mastodon (or your own role).
2. As the mastodon user (su -s /bin/sh mastodon):
       /usr/lib/mastodon/run bundle exec rails mastodon:setup
   It asks for the domain, database, Redis, SMTP and the admin account, writes
   /opt/mastodon/.env.production (Rails reads it itself; move it to
   /etc/mastodon/env.production if you prefer, the run script loads that too)
   and creates the tables. The assets are already built in the package.
   Example file: /usr/share/doc/mastodon/env.production.example.
3. nginx with TLS: /usr/share/doc/mastodon/nginx-mastodon.conf (example).
4. dinitctl enable mastodon-web mastodon-sidekiq mastodon-streaming
The domain (LOCAL_DOMAIN) cannot be changed after the first federation.
